jitterNameShadows -- a user's action named like one of incant/kantJitter's own names is found in that name's place.
kiT and kiIn are locals of the jitter's action krInside (kfP of krFetch, and so on). A fixture that includes kantJitter
and defines its own action kiT, then writes kiT at its top level, hands over the jitter's local, not its action. Nothing
says so and the run exits 0.
MEASURED 2026-11-17, kant, bare build, by this file: BEFORE krInside has run, kiT and kiIn name the file's own actions.
AFTER one call of krInside they name what its locals hold (taG, instructTypE). So the local is minted when the jitter's
action first runs, and from then on it is found ahead of the user's action of the same name. jsOther, a name the
jitter does not use, is unmoved (the control).
Found 2026-11-17 writing incant/pop/kantCondT (SEQ 675): kwCompile(kiT) answered "REFUSED taG -- kwCompile: the action
has no built chain", the action then ran interpreted with the right values, and only the count of compiles was short.
The fixture's actions were renamed (iq, wq, fq ...) and its notes say why.

Not measured: where the minted local sits and why it is found first (the KantJitter registry ahead of the user's on
the search list is the obvious suspect, not read). Not measured either: whether the locals of any included
incantation's actions (utilities, unitTests) do the same, which would make it a fact about locals and not the jitter.

